            <ArticleTitle>The presence of Chlamydia pneumoniae in atherosclerotic plaques--a report of three cases of ischaemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The report presents three cases of ischaemic heart disease in which Chlamydia pneumoniae infections were detected first serologically, later the bacteria were shown in atherosclerotic plaques with electron microscopy, and finally C. pneumoniae strains were isolated from the tissues.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
